  "title": "visStim",
  "description": "Electrocorticography (ECoG) recordings from 20 C57BL/6 mice in three cohorts: blinking light only, transcranial diagnostic ultrasound (tDUS) only, and combined tDUS with light. The dataset was collected to test how tDUS modulates the visual cortex's response to external visual stimulation. It includes raw, event-triggered, and processed ECoG data.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG electrodes targeted the visual and somatosensory cortices. Signals were recorded at 20 kS/s with LabChart and filtered at 5-55 Hz. Mice received 10-second blinking light events and tDUS delivered through a P21x5-1 scan head on a Sonosite MicroMaxx system. RMS values were normalized to baseline and analyzed in MATLAB.",
